   "caption": "Effect of different treatments on fire blight canker extension in ‘Gala’ apple (Malus domestica) shoots inoculated with Erwinia amylovora strain Ea06 (1 × 10 9 CFU/mL). Bars represent the mean percentage of canker extension measured two weeks post-inoculation. Treatments included streptomycin, salicylic acid applied weekly or biweekly, a combination of salicylic acid and streptomycin, and an infected untreated control. The combination treatment showed the greatest reduction in canker development compared with all other treatments. Bars with different letters indicate statistically significant differences according to Duncan’s multiple range least significant difference (LSD) test at p ≤ 0.05.",
